  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "Let \\(R=gS-4.\\) When \\(S=8,\\) \\(R=16.\\) When \\(S=10,\\) \\(R\\) is equal to:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(11\\)",
    "B": "\\(14\\)",
    "C": "\\(20\\)",
    "D": "\\(21\\)",
    "E": "None of these answers"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "First use the known pair \\(S=8\\), \\(R=16\\) to determine the constant \\(g\\). Substitution into \\(R=gS-4\\) gives\n\\[\n16=8g-4,\n\\qquad 20=8g,\n\\qquad g=\\frac52.\n\\]\nNow the same formula determines \\(R\\) when \\(S=10\\):\n\\[\nR=\\frac52\\cdot 10-4=25-4=21.\n\\]\nThus \\(\\boxed{21}\\) is choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
